WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.338 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: THE ELEPHANT.</i>

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:09.342 line:0%
<i>THEIR EARS CAN BE OVER 1/6
THE SIZE OF THEIR ENTIRE BODY.</i>

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.879 line:0%
<i>BUT YOU'RE ABOUT TO
FIND OUT HOW THEY CAN HEAR</i>

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.414 line:0%
<i>WITH THEIR FEET.</i>

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.850 line:0%
LAWRENCE: THEY'RE JUST
SORT OF MIND BLOWING.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.985 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: PLUS, CATS!</i>

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.821 line:0%
<i>THEY'RE THE MOST
POPULAR PET IN AMERICA.</i>

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:25.925 line:0%
<i>BUT THEIR PURRS MAY HELP KEEP
ASTRONAUTS ALIVE IN SPACE.</i>

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.762 line:0%
NATALIA: CATS IN SPACE!

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.465 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: AND THE OCTOPUS.</i>

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:36.569 line:0%
<i>IT'S BEEN ON THE PLANET
FOR OVER 90 MILLION YEARS.</i>

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.405 line:0%
<i>BUT CAN THIS CREATURE
FROM THE PAST ACTUALLY</i>

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:41.307 line:0%
<i>PREDICT THE FUTURE?</i>

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.843 line:0%
ROGER: IF YOU PUT A HUMAN
IN AN OCTOPUS ENVIRONMENT,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.413 line:0%
IT WOULDN'T SURVIVE
EVEN A DAY PROBABLY.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.521 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: THIS IS WHERE
SAVAGE MEETS SCIENCE...</i>

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.690 line:0%
<i>AND WILD BECOMES "WOW."</i>

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:03.463 line:0%
<i>THIS IS, "EVERYTHING YOU
DIDN'T KNOW ABOUT ANIMALS."</i>

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:13.406 line:0%
<i>IT'S HEART ALONE WEIGHS MORE
THAN A FIVE YEAR OLD CHILD.</i>

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.643 line:0%
<i>IF IT WERE STANDING
IN NEW YORK...</i>

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:20.080 line:0%
<i>IT COULD HEAR A
RAINSTORM IN PHILLY.</i>

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.317 line:0%
<i>JUST FOUR HOURS MOVING IN
THE HOT SUN COULD KILL IT...</i>

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:27.220 line:0%
<i>IF NOT FOR A
SECRET IN ITS EARS.</i>

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:31.491 line:0%
<i>IT'S STRONG ENOUGH TO
PUSH A TWO TON TRUCK...</i>

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:36.162 line:0%
<i>AND SMART ENOUGH TO
PAINT A PICTURE...</i>

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.499 line:0%
<i>IT IS THE ELEPHANT.</i>

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.306 line:0%
<i>SOUTH AFRICA.</i>

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.642 line:0%
<i>A BABY ELEPHANT HAS FALLEN
INTO A WATERING HOLE.</i>

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.881 line:0%
<i>TRAGEDY COULD BE
CLOSE AT HAND.</i>

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.084 line:0%
<i>BUT LOOK CAREFULLY...</i>

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:03.022 line:0%
<i>SUDDENLY, THE COMMUNITY OF
ELEPHANTS RUSHES TO THE RESCUE;</i>

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:06.659 line:0%
<i>IT'S NOW A GROUP EFFORT
TO GET THIS BABY TO SAFETY,</i>

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.062 line:0%
<i>BUT HOW?</i>

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:12.031 line:0%
CAITLIN: YOU DON'T
SEE THEM SIGNALING.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.433 line:0%
THEY JUST KNOW.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.736 line:0%
THEY JUST GET IN THERE,
GET DOWN ON THEIR KNEES,

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.806 line:0%
PULL THE BABY OUT.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:23.076 line:0%
ELEPHANTS ARE JUST AMAZING.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.181 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: NOT ONLY
ARE THEY AMAZING BUT</i>

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.749 line:0%
<i>THEY'RE ALSO SMART...</i>

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.318 line:0%
<i>THEY HAVE BEEN OBSERVED
DOING ADDITION WITH OVER 90%</i>

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.688 line:0%
<i>ACCURACY AND KEEP TRACK
OF MORE THAN 30 FAMILY</i>

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:38.291 line:0%
<i>MEMBERS AT ONCE.</i>

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:43.530 line:0%
<i>IN FACT, IN A LOT OF WAYS,
ELEPHANT'S SEEM MORE</i>

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.732 line:0%
<i>ADVANCED THAN US...</i>

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:51.371 line:0%
<i>STARTING WITH THE LARGEST BRAIN
OF ANY LAND MAMMAL ALIVE...</i>

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:56.109 line:0%
<i>IT'S UP TO 10 POUNDS
HEAVIER THAN OUR OWN.</i>

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.545 line:0%
<i>BUT IT'S WHAT'S
INSIDE THAT COUNTS.</i>

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.782 line:0%
<i>AN ELEPHANT'S TEMPORAL LOBES</i>

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.851 line:0%
<i>TAKE UP 45% OF THEIR ENTIRE</i>

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:08.188 line:0%
<i>BRAIN COMPARED TO OUR 20%.</i>

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:11.090 line:0%
<i>THAT'S WHAT GIVES THEM
THEIR FAMOUS MEMORIES.</i>

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.729 line:0%
<i>BUT THAT BIGGER TEMPORAL
LOBE ALSO HELPS THE ELEPHANT</i>

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.765 line:0%
<i>PROCESS SOUNDS...</i>

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.701 line:0%
<i>AND WHEN IT COMES TO HEARING,
THEY HAVE ABILITIES THAT WALK</i>

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.469 line:0%
<i>ALL OVER OURS.</i>

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:27.040 line:0%
<i>BECAUSE THEY CAN ACTUALLY
HEAR WITH THEIR FEET!</i>

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.214 line:0%
<i>HERE'S HOW IT WORKS: ELEPHANTS
SOMETIMES COMMUNICATE WITH</i>

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:37.951 line:0%
<i>EACH OTHER OVER LONG
DISTANCES BY STOMPING,</i>

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:42.188 line:0%
<i>OR SENDING LOW FREQUENCY
RUMBLES THROUGH THE GROUND.</i>

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:45.491 line:0%
<i>THESE SEISMIC WAVES THEN
TRAVEL THROUGH THE EARTH AND</i>

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:48.161 line:0%
<i>GET PICKED UP BY VIBRATION
SENSITIVE CELLS IN AN</i>

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:51.030
<i>ELEPHANT'S FEET CALLED
"PACINIAN CORPSUCLES."</i>

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:55.835 line:0%
<i>THEN, THOSE CELLS SEND A NERVE
IMPULSE STRAIGHT TO THE BRAIN.</i>

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.905 line:0%
CAITLIN: SO YOU'RE
NOT ACTUALLY HEARING

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.540 line:0%
THROUGH YOUR EAR.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.042 line:0%
YOU'RE HEARING DIRECTLY TO
THE BRAIN THROUGH THESE NERVE

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:06.746 line:0%
IMPULSES COMING FROM
THESE VIBRA-TACTILE CELLS.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.685 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: IN ADDITION TO
HELPING THE ELEPHANT KEEP</i>

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:16.155 line:0%
<i>TRACK OF FAR-FLUNG
FAMILY MEMBERS...</i>

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:19.759 line:0%
<i>THIS SEISMIC SENSITIVITY MAY
AID IN THE ELEPHANT'S SEARCH</i>

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.595 line:0%
<i>FOR LIFE SUSTAINING WATER.</i>

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:29.035 line:0%
<i>ONE STUDY ANALYZED DATA
FROM GPS TRACKING DEVICES OF</i>

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:32.939 line:0%
<i>FOURTEEN DIFFERENT
HERDS OVER SEVEN YEARS.</i>

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.409 line:0%
<i>THEIR FINDINGS SUGGEST THAT
ELEPHANTS CAN TELL WHEN A</i>

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:40.647 line:0%
<i>STORM IS APPROACHING EVEN
IF IT'S 150 MILES AWAY!</i>

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:45.551 line:0%
CAITLIN: WE THINK THEY'RE
DETECTING THUNDER IN THE GROUND.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.388 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: YOUR LOCAL
WEATHERMAN COULD LEARN A</i>

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.990 line:0%
<i>THING OR TWO.</i>

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:56.062 line:0%
<i>AND THAT MAY NOT
BE SO FAR-FETCHED.</i>

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:59.165 line:0%
<i>HUMANS HAVE THE SAME VIBRATION
SENSITIVE CELLS AS ELEPHANTS</i>

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:02.902 line:0%
<i>IN OUR OWN HANDS AND FEET AND
HIGH-TECH HEARING AIDS ARE NOW</i>

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.805 line:0%
<i>BEING DEVELOPED THAT UTILIZE
THEM IN THE SAME WAY THE</i>

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:08.841 line:0%
<i>ELEPHANT DOES.</i>

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.480 line:0%
<i>OF COURSE ELEPHANTS ALSO
USE THEIR FEET IN THE MORE</i>

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.317 line:0%
<i>TRADITIONAL WAY.</i>

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:22.355 line:0%
<i>AN AVERAGE AFRICAN ELEPHANT
CAN COVER 50 MILES A DAY.</i>

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:26.092 line:0%
<i>THAT'S OVER 18,000
MILES A YEAR...</i>

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:28.428 line:0%
<i>ROUGHLY SIX AND A HALF
TIMES THE DISTANCE FROM</i>

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.963 line:0%
<i>NEW YORK TO CALIFORNIA.</i>

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.667 line:0%
<i>IF YOU WERE TO RUN
THAT MUCH IN A YEAR,</i>

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.770 line:0%
<i>YOU'D GO THROUGH UP TO
60 PAIRS OF SHOES...</i>

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.807 line:0%
<i>IF YOUR LEGS DIDN'T
GIVE OUT FIRST.</i>

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.310 line:0%
<i>BUT ELEPHANTS HAVE AN
EXTRA SUPPORT SYSTEM BUILT</i>

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:48.514 line:0%
<i>RIGHT INTO THEIR FEET.</i>

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.020 line:0%
LAWRENCE: THEY ACTUALLY WALK
ON THE TIPS OF THEIR TOES.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.023 line:0%
BUT THEY SORT OF HAVE THIS
FAT FILLED HEEL THAT ACTUALLY

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.825 line:0%
SUPPORTS THEIR WEIGHT.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:01.828 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: AND
INSIDE THAT FAT PAD?</i>

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:05.798 line:0%
<i>IT'S THE ELEPHANT'S
OWN STILLETO HEEL...</i>

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:08.401 line:0%
<i>A BACKWARD FACING SIXTH TOE
THAT HELPS KEEP THE ELEPHANT</i>

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:12.505 line:0%
<i>FROM KEELING OVER DURING LONG
TREKS FOR WATER AND FOOD!</i>

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:16.976 line:0%
<i>THIS EXTRA "TOE" FORMS AS A
SMALL ROD OF CARTILAGE THAT</i>

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:20.146 line:0%
<i>GROWS LONGER AND STRONGER.</i>

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.783 line:0%
<i>AS THE ELEPHANT AGES,
THE DIGIT EVENTUALLY</i>

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:26.619 line:0%
<i>TRANSFORMS INTO BONE.</i>

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.389 line:0%
<i>IT'S LIKE A KICKSTAND
BUILT RIGHT INTO THE FOOT.</i>

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:31.758 line:0%
<i>AND WHO COULDN'T
USE ONE OF THOSE?</i>

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:40.433 line:0%
<i>DISNEY DID A PRETTY GOOD JOB
OF MAKING ELEPHANT EARS FLY</i>

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:43.369 line:0%
<i>BUT EVEN IN REAL LIFE,
THEY'RE PRETTY AMAZING.</i>

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:47.774 line:0%
<i>IN FACT, THEY DO A LOT MORE
FOR THE ELEPHANT THAN OUR EARS</i>

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.776 line:0%
<i>DO FOR US.</i>

00:06:49.776 --> 00:06:52.311 line:0%
<i>THEY MAY EVEN HELP
KEEP THEM ALIVE.</i>

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:59.051 line:0%
<i>WHERE SOME ELEPHANTS LIVE,
TEMPERATURES CAN REACH A</i>

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:03.189 line:0%
<i>SCORCHING HOT 122
DEGREES FAHRENHEIT.</i>

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:06.192 line:0%
<i>BECAUSE OF THIS
FIERY ENVIRONMENT,</i>

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:09.595 line:0%
<i>ELEPHANTS LIVE IN CONSTANT
DANGER OF OVERHEATING.</i>

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:12.398 line:0%
<i>JUST FOUR HOURS OF MOVING
IN THE HOT SUN IS ENOUGH TO</i>

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:15.067 line:0%
<i>DO AN ELEPHANT IN.</i>

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.540 line:0%
<i>YOU MAY THINK THEY BEAT
THE HEAT BY ROLLING AROUND</i>

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:21.941 line:0%
<i>IN THE MUD.</i>

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:24.777 line:0%
<i>BUT THAT'S ONLY
PART OF THE STORY.</i>

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:27.447 line:0%
<i>BELIEVE IT OR NOT, ONE
OF THEIR MOST IMPORTANT</i>

00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:29.215 line:0%
<i>MECHANISMS FOR CHILLING OUT...</i>

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:31.317 line:0%
<i>IS INSIDE THE EARS.</i>

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:35.154 line:0%
<i>HERE'S HOW IT WORKS:
THE SKIN ON AN ELEPHANT'S EAR</i>

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.856 line:0%
<i>IS VERY THIN...</i>

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:39.091 line:0%
<i>JUST ONE TO TWO MILLIMETERS.</i>

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:41.627 line:0%
<i>BARELY THICKER THAN A PENNY.</i>

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:44.130 line:0%
<i>LOOK EVEN CLOSER AND YOU'LL
SEE AN INTRICATE NETWORK OF</i>

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.066 line:0%
<i>BLOOD VESSELS JUST
BELOW THE SURFACE.</i>

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:50.069 line:0%
<i>WHEN AN ELEPHANT
FLAPS ITS EARS,</i>

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:52.772 line:0%
<i>AIR FLOWS OVER THESE VESSELS,
COOLING THE BLOOD WITHIN.</i>

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:58.010 line:0%
<i>THEN, LIKE FREON IN
AN AIR CONDITIONER,</i>

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:01.547 line:0%
<i>THE COOLED BLOOD MOVES
THROUGH THE REST OF ITS</i>

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:04.417 line:0%
<i>CIRCULATORY SYSTEM.</i>

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.919 line:0%
<i>THAT REDUCES ITS CORE
TEMPERATURE BY AS MUCH</i>

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:09.622 line:0%
<i>AS 10 DEGREES.</i>

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:13.159 line:0%
<i>YOU MIGHT EVEN CALL THEM
EARS "EAR CONDITIONERS."</i>

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:18.498 line:0%
<i>USING THEIR EARS,
AN ELEPHANT CAN COOL ALL THE</i>

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:22.668 line:0%
<i>BLOOD IN THEIR BODY
IN JUST TWENTY MINUTES.</i>

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:34.146 line:0%
<i>THE ELEPHANT IS THE ONLY
MAMMAL, BESIDES HUMANS,</i>

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:36.582 line:0%
<i>THAT HAS A CHIN.</i>

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:38.684 line:0%
<i>ITS FOOTPATHS ARE SO MASSIVE;</i>

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:41.921 line:0%
<i>SATELLITES CAN
SEE THEM FROM SPACE.</i>

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:46.659 line:0%
<i>IT IS THE LARGEST
ANIMAL ON LAND AND YET,</i>

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:50.096 line:0%
<i>IF YOU WANTED TO CATCH A
GLIMPSE OF ANCIENT ELEPHANTS,</i>

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:53.733 line:0%
<i>YOUR BEST BET
MIGHT'VE BEEN BY BOAT.</i>

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:58.337 line:0%
CAITLIN: ELEPHANTS HAVE AN
AQUATIC ANCESTRY AND WHEN YOU

00:08:58.337 --> 00:09:00.873 line:0%
SEE AN ELEPHANT IN
WATER, IT SEEMS OBVIOUS.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:04.510 line:0%
THEY CAN SWIM IN IT, THEY CAN
USE THEIR TRUNK AS A SNORKEL

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.512 line:0%
AND THEY SWIM ACROSS THE
RIVER COMPLETELY SUBMERGED.

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:10.182 line:0%
AND THEY'RE VERY
GOOD SWIMMERS.

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:13.519 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: THEY MIGHT EVEN
SHARE A COMMON ANCESTOR WITH</i>

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:17.490 line:0%
<i>THE ENTIRELY AQUATIC
MANATEE AND DUGONG.</i>

00:09:21.327 --> 00:09:24.697 line:0%
<i>BUT IT'S COME A LONG WAY SINCE
SWIMMING THE RIVERS OF THE</i>

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:29.402 line:0%
<i>PAST AND AS WE'VE SEEN,
IT'S EVOLVED INTO A CREATURE</i>

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:34.307 line:0%
<i>THAT IN SOME WAYS MAY
BE MORE ADVANCED THAN US.</i>

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:39.879 line:0%
<i>BUT THERE IS ONE THING THAT
TERRIFIES THIS COMPLICATED</i>

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:43.182 line:0%
<i>GIANT AND IT'S EVEN
SMALLER THAN A BASKETBALL.</i>

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:46.986 line:0%
<i>IS IT: A,
A SKITTERING FIELD MOUSE?</i>

00:09:47.787 --> 00:09:50.089 line:0%
<i>B, A THORNY BRANCH?</i>

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:52.725 line:0%
<i>OR C, A BUZZING BEE?</i>

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:56.062 line:0%
<i>PLUS, FIND OUT WHY ROBOTICS
ENGINEERS ARE DROOLING OVER</i>

00:09:56.062 --> 00:09:58.898 line:0%
<i>THE ELEPHANT'S TRUNK!</i>

00:10:05.972 --> 00:10:10.276 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: THE ELEPHANT, AN
ANIMAL AS ODD AS IT IS EPIC</i>

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:14.413 line:0%
<i>BUT AS IMPRESSIVE AS THEY
ARE, THERE IS ONE THING THAT</i>

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:16.582 line:0%
<i>TERRIFIES THE ELEPHANT
AND IT'S EVEN SMALLER</i>

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:18.918 line:0%
<i>THAN A BASKETBALL.</i>

00:10:19.151 --> 00:10:22.121 line:0%
<i>IS IT: A,
A SKITTERING FIELD MOUSE?</i>

00:10:23.022 --> 00:10:25.424 line:0%
<i>B, A THORNY BRANCH?</i>

00:10:25.424 --> 00:10:28.928 line:0%
<i>OR C, A BUZZING BEE?</i>

00:10:28.928 --> 00:10:32.798 line:0%
<i>THE CORRECT ANSWER
IS "C," THE BEE.</i>

00:10:36.669 --> 00:10:39.639 line:0%
<i>AS GIANT AS THEY ARE, THE
ELEPHANT HAS NO DEFENSES</i>

00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:43.109 line:0%
<i>AGAINST TINY BEES GETTING
INSIDE THEIR SENSATIVE TRUNKS</i>

00:10:43.109 --> 00:10:45.945 line:0%
<i>AND STINGING.</i>

00:10:46.212 --> 00:10:48.581 line:0%
<i>AND WITH THEIR
MASSIVE MEMORIES,</i>

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:51.517 line:0%
<i>THAT'S A STING
THEY NEVER FORGET.</i>

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:57.123 line:0%
<i>ELEPHANTS ARE SO SCARED
OF GETTING STUNG,</i>

00:10:57.123 --> 00:11:00.926 line:0%
<i>FARMERS IN AFRICA ACTUALLY USE
FENCES MADE OF BEE HIVES TO</i>

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:04.864 line:0%
<i>KEEP THE BEHEMOTHS FROM
DESTROYING THEIR CROPS.</i>

00:11:06.532 --> 00:11:09.869 line:0%
<i>SO THAT'S ONE WAY WE HAVE
A LEG UP ON DUMBO BUT THE</i>

00:11:09.869 --> 00:11:12.371 line:0%
<i>ELEPHANT ISN'T STOPPING YET.</i>

00:11:12.638 --> 00:11:14.674 line:0%
<i>AND WHEN IT COMES
TO SHOWING US UP,</i>

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:17.109 line:0%
<i>NO PART OF THE ELEPHANT
