<i>A, SHAVE THEIR
OWN EYEBROWS...</i>

00:21:53.845 --> 00:21:55.814 line:0%
<i>B, CARVE A FIGURINE,</i>

00:21:55.814 --> 00:21:58.784 line:0%
<i>OR C, STAY AWAKE
UNTIL SUNRISE?</i>

00:21:59.184 --> 00:22:00.552 line:0%
<i>GIVE UP?</i>

00:22:00.552 --> 00:22:03.155 line:0%
<i>BELIEVE IT OR NOT, ACCORDING
TO THE ANCIENT HISTORIAN</i>

00:22:03.155 --> 00:22:06.725 line:0%
<i>HERODOTUS, WHEN EGYPTIAN CATS
PASSED ON TO THE AFTERLIFE,</i>

00:22:06.725 --> 00:22:08.493 line:0%
<i>THE ENTIRE HOUSEHOLD
WOULD OFTEN SHAVE THEIR</i>

00:22:08.493 --> 00:22:11.697 line:0%
<i>EYEBROWS IN MOURNING.</i>

00:22:11.697 --> 00:22:14.366 line:0%
<i>THAT'S KITTY COMMITMENT.</i>

00:22:16.268 --> 00:22:18.203 line:0%
<i>NOW, WE GET BACK
INTO OUR EIGHT,</i>

00:22:18.203 --> 00:22:21.807 line:0%
<i>LESSER-KNOWN FACTS ABOUT
THE CAT ON YOUR LAP.</i>

00:22:22.074 --> 00:22:25.577 line:0%
<i>FOR CAT FACT FOUR, WE'RE
TAKING THINGS UP A NOTCH...</i>

00:22:25.577 --> 00:22:28.046 line:0%
<i>OVER 300 FEET UP TO BE EXACT.</i>

00:22:35.787 --> 00:22:38.590 line:0%
<i>INCREDIBLY, CATS HAVE BEEN
KNOWN TO SURVIVE FALLS FROM AS</i>

00:22:38.590 --> 00:22:41.126 line:0%
<i>HIGH UP AS THE
STATUE OF LIBERTY.</i>

00:22:41.126 --> 00:22:42.494 line:0%
<i>BUT HOW?</i>

00:22:42.494 --> 00:22:44.863 line:0%
MIKKEL: CATS DO NOT ALWAYS
LAND ON THEIR FEET BUT

00:22:44.863 --> 00:22:48.033 line:0%
THEY DO HAVE PRETTY AMAZING
KIND OF NINJA SKILLS

00:22:48.033 --> 00:22:50.635 line:0%
WHEN THEY'RE FALLING.

00:22:53.338 --> 00:22:55.707 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: TO UNDERSTAND
HOW THIS WORKS,</i>

00:22:55.707 --> 00:22:58.477 line:0%
<i>LET'S TAKE A LOOK AT
THE BACKBONE OF THE CAT.</i>

00:22:58.477 --> 00:23:01.480 line:0%
<i>CATS HAVE 30 VERTEBRAE
IN THEIR SPINES,</i>

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:03.382 line:0%
<i>COMPARED TO OUR 24.</i>

00:23:03.382 --> 00:23:06.818 line:0%
<i>THEY CAN BEND ALMOST
A FULL 180 DEGREES,</i>

00:23:06.818 --> 00:23:09.621 line:0%
<i>WHICH ALLOWS CATS TO ROTATE
AND RIGHT THEIR HEADS IN THE</i>

00:23:09.621 --> 00:23:13.692 line:0%
<i>AIR, THEN QUICKLY TWIST THE
REST OF THEIR BODIES AROUND.</i>

00:23:13.692 --> 00:23:16.862 line:0%
<i>AT THE SAME TIME, THE
FALLING CAT ARCHES ITS BACK,</i>

00:23:16.862 --> 00:23:21.233 line:0%
<i>WHICH DAMPENS THE FORCE OF
IMPACT AS IT HITS THE GROUND.</i>

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:24.403 line:0%
<i>CATS CAN MANIPULATE THEIR
BODIES TO LAND WITH A FORCE</i>

00:23:24.403 --> 00:23:27.839 line:0%
<i>FIVE TIMES LESS THAN AN
INANIMATE OBJECT DROPPED FROM</i>

00:23:27.839 --> 00:23:30.509 line:0%
<i>THE SAME HEIGHT.</i>

00:23:35.147 --> 00:23:38.850 line:0%
<i>AMAZINGLY ENOUGH, THE WAY A
CAT FALLS MAY INFLUENCE THE</i>

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.719 line:0%
<i>FUTURE OF FIRST AID.</i>

00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:43.288 line:0%
<i>RESEARCHERS AT GEORGIA TECH
ARE ACTUALLY STUDYING</i>

00:23:43.288 --> 00:23:46.691 line:0%
<i>THE DYNAMICS OF FALLING
CATS' FLEXIBLE SPINES</i>

00:23:46.691 --> 00:23:49.561 line:0%
<i>TO CREATE UNBREAKABLE,
SELF-RIGHTING ROBOTS FOR SEARCH</i>

00:23:49.561 --> 00:23:51.530 line:0%
<i>AND RESCUE MISSIONS.</i>

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:54.966 line:0%
<i>SO IN A WAY, CATS ARE TAKING
SOME OF THEIR NINE LIVES AND</i>

00:23:54.966 --> 00:23:57.569 line:0%
<i>GIVING THEM TO US.</i>

00:24:06.611 --> 00:24:10.015 line:0%
<i>BUT THERE'S MUCH MORE TO
A CAT THAN HOW IT FALLS.</i>

00:24:10.015 --> 00:24:15.253 line:0%
<i>FOR CAT FACT NUMBER FIVE, WE
EXPLORE THEIR "SUPER SENSES."</i>

00:24:16.855 --> 00:24:19.291 line:0%
<i>IT STARTS WITH THE EYES.</i>

00:24:19.291 --> 00:24:22.260 line:0%
<i>DOMESTIC CATS NEED JUST
ONE-SIXTH THE LIGHT THAT</i>

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:23.829 line:0%
<i>HUMANS NEED TO SEE.</i>

00:24:23.829 --> 00:24:26.398 line:0%
<i>SO WHEN WE SEE BLACKNESS...</i>

00:24:28.266 --> 00:24:32.337 line:0%
<i>THEY SEE EVERYTHING.</i>

00:24:34.072 --> 00:24:36.675 line:0%
<i>CATS ALSO HAVE
EXCELLENT HEARING.</i>

00:24:36.675 --> 00:24:38.977 line:0%
<i>BETTER THAN DOGS, EVEN.</i>

00:24:39.544 --> 00:24:43.748 line:0%
<i>THEY'RE CAPABLE OF HEARING
FREQUENCIES UP TO 85,000 HERTZ.</i>

00:24:43.748 --> 00:24:48.086 line:0%
<i>PERFECT FOR SENSING
SMALL THINGS OF BIG INTEREST.</i>

00:24:52.557 --> 00:24:55.193 line:0%
<i>BUT IN ADDITION
TO NIGHT VISION GOGGLES AND</i>

00:24:55.193 --> 00:24:56.595 line:0%
<i>SUPER SONIC EARS...</i>

00:24:56.595 --> 00:24:59.264 line:0%
<i>CATS ALSO HAVE
POWERFUL NOSES...</i>

00:24:59.264 --> 00:25:01.766 line:0%
<i>14 TIMES STRONGER
THAN OUR OWN.</i>

00:25:01.766 --> 00:25:04.236 line:0%
<i>AND THEY USE THOSE NOSES TO
SNIFF OUT ONE OF THEIR MOST</i>

00:25:04.236 --> 00:25:06.838 line:0%
<i>FAVORITE THINGS.</i>

00:25:11.943 --> 00:25:15.146 line:0%
<i>SOME CATS FALL INTO A
TRANCE WHEN THEY SMELL IT.</i>

00:25:15.146 --> 00:25:17.582 line:0%
<i>OTHERS GO CRAZY WITH DELIGHT.</i>

00:25:17.582 --> 00:25:18.917 line:0%
<i>IT'S STRONG.</i>

00:25:18.917 --> 00:25:20.218 line:0%
<i>IT'S EFFECTIVE.</i>

00:25:20.218 --> 00:25:22.821 line:0%
<i>IT'S CATNIP.</i>

00:25:24.322 --> 00:25:26.892 line:0%
<i>THOUGH IT SEEMS LIKE
SOME EXOTIC NARCOTIC,</i>

00:25:26.892 --> 00:25:30.395 line:0%
<i>CATNIP IS JUST AN HERB
IN THE MINT FAMILY.</i>

00:25:30.395 --> 00:25:32.697 line:0%
MIKKEL: SOME CATS ARE NOT
AFFECTED BY IT AT ALL.

00:25:32.697 --> 00:25:36.368 line:0%
BUT OTHER CATS, IT MAKES JUST
THIS GINORMOUS IMPACT ON THEM.

00:25:36.368 --> 00:25:39.037 line:0%
IT MAY BE LIKE KIND OF
MEOWY-WOWY FOR THEM WHERE

00:25:39.037 --> 00:25:41.840 line:0%
THEY'RE LIKE, "OH MAN,
THIS IS LIKE THE BEST."

00:25:44.643 --> 00:25:46.611 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: BUT
HOW DOES IT WORK?</i>

00:25:46.611 --> 00:25:49.714 line:0%
<i>THERE IS A CHEMICAL IN CATNIP
CALLED NEPETALACTONE THAT SOME</i>

00:25:49.714 --> 00:25:53.585 line:0%
<i>RESEARCHERS SPECULATE
MIMICS CAT PHEROMONES.</i>

00:25:55.820 --> 00:26:00.292 line:0%
<i>AND IT EVEN WORKS ON BIG CATS.</i>

00:26:00.292 --> 00:26:04.062 line:0%
MARTY: SOME CATS GO MILD
AND SOME CATS GO WILD.

00:26:04.696 --> 00:26:06.998 line:0%
SOME ARE SCREECHING,
RUNNING AROUND,

00:26:06.998 --> 00:26:08.600 line:0%
THEY'RE EVEN FLYING
UP IN THE AIR,

00:26:08.600 --> 00:26:09.968 line:0%
GRABBING IMAGINARY THINGS.

00:26:09.968 --> 00:26:12.804 line:0%
AND OTHERS JUST SIT
THERE AND SLOBBER.

00:26:12.804 --> 00:26:15.106 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: BUT THE MOST
AMAZING THING ABOUT CATNIP MAY</i>

00:26:15.106 --> 00:26:16.775 line:0%
<i>BE THAT IT'S
NOT JUST FOR CATS.</i>

00:26:16.775 --> 00:26:18.577 line:0%
<i>HUMANS CAN USE IT TOO!</i>

00:26:18.577 --> 00:26:22.080 line:0%
<i>AND THAT'S OUR SIXTH
AMAZING CAT FACT.</i>

00:26:26.284 --> 00:26:28.520 line:0%
<i>BELIEVE IT OR NOT,
CATNIP MAKES AN EXCELLENT</i>

00:26:28.520 --> 00:26:31.156 line:0%
<i>MOSQUITO REPELLENT.</i>

00:26:31.156 --> 00:26:33.558 line:0%
<i>ACCORDING TO SOME STUDIES,
IT'S ACTUALLY 10 TIMES MORE</i>

00:26:33.558 --> 00:26:35.427 line:0%
<i>POWERFUL THAN DEET.</i>

00:26:35.427 --> 00:26:38.663 line:0%
<i>SO USE A LITTLE CATNIP
AND LOSE THE MOSQUITOS.</i>

00:26:38.964 --> 00:26:41.866 line:0%
<i>YOU MAY, HOWEVER,
BE SWARMED BY CATS.</i>

00:26:48.073 --> 00:26:50.141 line:0%
<i>THERE'S AN OLD ENGLISH
PROVERB THAT STATES,</i>

00:26:50.141 --> 00:26:53.378 line:0%
<i>"IN A CAT'S EYE,
ALL THINGS BELONG TO CATS."</i>

00:26:53.378 --> 00:26:56.748 line:0%
<i>AND THAT MAY INCLUDE US!</i>

00:26:56.748 --> 00:27:00.652 line:0%
<i>WHICH MAY EXPLAIN OUR
AMAZING FACT NUMBER SEVEN:</i>

00:27:00.652 --> 00:27:04.422 line:0%
<i>OLDER CATS ONLY
MEOW FOR HUMANS.</i>

00:27:08.259 --> 00:27:10.862 line:0%
<i>WHILE KITTENS WILL MEOW TO
LET THEIR MOM'S KNOW THEY'RE</i>

00:27:10.862 --> 00:27:15.333 line:0%
<i>HUNGRY, ONCE THEY GROW UP,
THAT MEOW IS ALL FOR US.</i>

00:27:15.333 --> 00:27:17.969 line:0%
<i>SOME CATS EVEN A HAVE A
SPECIFIC "HUNGER" CRY THAT WE</i>

00:27:17.969 --> 00:27:21.306 line:0%
<i>MAY BE HARDWIRED
TO RESPOND TO.</i>

00:27:22.073 --> 00:27:24.776 line:0%
MIKKEL: IT'S BOTH A MEOW
