00:32:31.616 --> 00:32:34.018
<i>THEY'RE CALLED
"CHROMATOPHORES."</i>

00:32:34.018 --> 00:32:35.586
<i>EACH OF THESE
CHROMATOPHORES IS SURROUNDED</i>

00:32:35.586 --> 00:32:37.789 line:0%
<i>BY MUSCLE FIBERS.</i>

00:32:37.789 --> 00:32:40.158 line:0%
<i>WHEN THEY CONTRACT,
THEY OPEN UP THE BAG AND</i>

00:32:40.158 --> 00:32:41.859 line:0%
<i>REVEAL A NEW COLOR.</i>

00:32:41.859 --> 00:32:44.829 line:0%
<i>AND WHEN THE MUSCLES RELAX,
IT SNAPS BACK IN AND</i>

00:32:44.829 --> 00:32:48.666 line:0%
<i>HIDES THE COLOR.</i>

00:32:49.367 --> 00:32:52.003 line:0%
<i>BUT HOW CAN THE OCTOPUS
CREATE SUCH AN AMAZING ARRAY</i>

00:32:52.003 --> 00:32:55.039 line:0%
<i>OF COLORFUL
PATTERNS SO QUICKLY?</i>

00:32:55.406 --> 00:32:58.376 line:0%
ROGER: TO LOOK LIKE
600 OR 1,000 KINDS OF PLANTS

00:32:58.376 --> 00:33:00.478 line:0%
AND ANIMALS
WITHIN A THIRD OF A SECOND

00:33:00.478 --> 00:33:02.246 line:0%
IS TOTAL NONSENSE.

00:33:04.549 --> 00:33:06.617 line:0%
IT'S IMPOSSIBLE,
YOU CAN'T DO IT.

00:33:06.617 --> 00:33:08.419 line:0%
THERE HAS TO BE A SHORT CUT.

00:33:08.419 --> 00:33:11.689 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: HERE'S THE SHORTCUT:
THE OCTOPUS HAS FIGURED OUT</i>

00:33:11.689 --> 00:33:14.692 line:0%
<i>THAT THERE ARE REALLY ONLY A
FEW BASIC PATTERNS IT NEEDS TO</i>

00:33:14.692 --> 00:33:17.161 line:0%
<i>KNOW TO BLEND INTO THE
NATURAL ENVIRONMENT.</i>

00:33:19.197 --> 00:33:21.432 line:0%
<i>UNIFORM, LIKE WHAT
YOU MIGHT SEE ON A ROCK</i>

00:33:21.432 --> 00:33:23.434 line:0%
<i>WITH NO CONTRAST...</i>

00:33:23.434 --> 00:33:27.638 line:0%
<i>MOTTLED, LIKE THE GRAVELLY
SUBSTRATE OF THE OCEAN FLOOR</i>

00:33:27.638 --> 00:33:31.075 line:0%
<i>AND DISRUPTIVE, WHICH MAKES
THE OCTOPUS UNRECOGNIZABLE IN</i>

00:33:31.075 --> 00:33:34.312 line:0%
<i>SHADOWY REEFS.</i>

00:33:34.312 --> 00:33:37.081 line:0%
<i>SO INSTEAD OF HAVING TO
INSTANTLY MATCH EVERY LITTLE</i>

00:33:37.081 --> 00:33:41.185 line:0%
<i>PIECE OF ITS ENVIRONMENT,
ALL THE OCTOPUS NEEDS IS A</i>

00:33:41.185 --> 00:33:45.323 line:0%
<i>QUICK VISUAL CUE TO TURN ON
ONE OF THE 3 PATTERNS</i>

00:33:45.323 --> 00:33:47.325 line:0%
<i>AND THEN FINE TUNE.</i>

00:33:47.325 --> 00:33:49.927 line:0%
ROGER: SO ALL THEY HAVE
TO REALLY DO, IS SETTLE,

00:33:49.927 --> 00:33:52.530 line:0%
LOOK AROUND THEM, IF THE CUE
AROUND THEM IS FOR PATTERN 2,

00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:54.732 line:0%
THEY PUT ON PATTERN 2.

00:33:54.732 --> 00:33:56.601 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: IT'S LIKE BEING
ABLE TO INSTANTLY CHANGE YOUR</i>

00:33:56.601 --> 00:33:59.470 line:0%
<i>OUTFIT TO MATCH ANY OCCASION.</i>

00:34:07.045 --> 00:34:10.681 line:0%
<i>IT'S A COMPLEX SURVIVAL
TECHNIQUE FOR SURE.</i>

00:34:10.915 --> 00:34:13.785 line:0%
<i>BUT THE OCTOPUSES NEXT
SKILL TO STAY ALIVE MAY BE</i>

00:34:13.785 --> 00:34:16.287 line:0%
<i>EVEN MORE AMAZING....</i>

00:34:16.287 --> 00:34:18.956 line:0%
<i>WATCH THIS OCTOPUS
ONE MORE TIME.</i>

00:34:19.257 --> 00:34:23.027 align:end position:100% line:0%
<i>NOTICE HOW IT'S NOT JUST HIS
COLOR AND PATTERN THAT CHANGES.</i>

00:34:23.027 --> 00:34:26.297 line:0%
<i>BUT ALSO... HIS TEXTURE.</i>

00:34:31.602 --> 00:34:34.939 line:0%
<i>A BIOLOGICAL STRUCTURE UNDER
THE SKIN ALLOWS THE OCTOPUS</i>

00:34:34.939 --> 00:34:36.908 line:0%
<i>TO MORPH IN 3-D.</i>

00:34:39.277 --> 00:34:43.247 line:0%
<i>HERE'S HOW IT WORKS: RINGS
OF MUSCLES ON THE OCTOPUS'S</i>

00:34:43.247 --> 00:34:46.250 line:0%
<i>SKIN CONTRACT,
SQUEEZING IT INTO LUMPS.</i>

00:34:47.385 --> 00:34:50.788 line:0%
<i>INSIDE THE LUMPS, ANOTHER
SET OF MUSCLES TIGHTEN UP,</i>

00:34:50.788 --> 00:34:54.025 line:0%
<i>PULLING THE BLOBS OF
SKIN INTO DEFINED SHAPES.</i>

00:34:54.025 --> 00:34:56.094 line:0%
<i>WHEN THE OCTOPUS
WANTS TO SMOOTH OUT,</i>

00:34:56.094 --> 00:34:59.063 line:0%
<i>A THIRD GROUP OF MUSCLES
PULLS THE SKIN FLAT AGAIN.</i>

00:35:02.066 --> 00:35:04.469 line:0%
ROGER: THERE'S NO OTHER
ANIMAL ON EARTH THAT CAN CHANGE

00:35:04.469 --> 00:35:07.371 line:0%
THE THREE DIMENSIONALITY
OF THEIR SKIN.

00:35:07.371 --> 00:35:10.174 line:0%
SO YOU EITHER GOT
IT OR YOU DON'T.

00:35:15.646 --> 00:35:18.149 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: THE OCTOPUS'S
ANCESTORS HAVE BEEN TRYING TO</i>

00:35:18.149 --> 00:35:22.553 line:0%
<i>SURVIVE IN THE OCEAN FOR
UP TO 500 MILLION YEARS.</i>

00:35:22.553 --> 00:35:25.389 line:0%
<i>THAT'S OLDER THAN FISH!</i>

00:35:25.389 --> 00:35:28.092 line:0%
<i>BACK THEN, IT MIGHT HAVE HAD
EXTRA PROTECTION IN THE FORM</i>

00:35:28.092 --> 00:35:30.561 line:0%
<i>OF A HARD OUTER SHELL.</i>

00:35:30.561 --> 00:35:33.064 line:0%
<i>LIKE THE NAUTILUS OF TODAY.</i>

00:35:33.431 --> 00:35:36.467 line:0%
<i>BUT SOMEWHERE ALONG THE WAY,
THE OCTOPUS TRADED ITS ARMOR</i>

00:35:36.467 --> 00:35:39.070 line:0%
<i>FOR MORE ADVANCED
SURVIVAL TECHNIQUES...</i>

00:35:41.739 --> 00:35:43.975 line:0%
<i>WHICH ISN'T TO SAY THEY
WON'T BORROW SOMEBODY ELSE'S</i>

00:35:43.975 --> 00:35:46.344 line:0%
<i>SHELL IN A PINCH.</i>

00:35:47.278 --> 00:35:49.113 line:0%
NATALIA: I JUST LIKE THE
IDEA THAT THEY COULD JUST BE

00:35:49.113 --> 00:35:50.681 line:0%
WEARING THE CLAM,
LIKE AS IF THAT IS GOING TO

00:35:50.681 --> 00:35:51.983 line:0%
MASK THEM COMPLETELY.

00:35:51.983 --> 00:35:54.252 line:0%
"NOTHING TO SEE HERE FOLKS."

00:35:54.252 --> 00:35:55.987 line:0%
♪ DOO, DEE, DOO,
DEE, DOO, DOO, ♪

00:35:55.987 --> 00:35:57.655 line:0%
♪ DOO, DEE, DOO,
DEE, DOO, DEE, DOO. ♪♪

00:35:57.655 --> 00:36:00.024 line:0%
<i>[LAUGHS].</i>

00:36:00.358 --> 00:36:03.628 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: SO FAR WE'VE BROKEN
DOWN THE OCTOPUS'S ABILITY</i>

00:36:03.628 --> 00:36:07.331 line:0%
<i>TO CHANGE COLOR AND SHAPE
IN ORDER TO STAY ALIVE.</i>

00:36:07.798 --> 00:36:10.401 line:0%
<i>BUT THERE'S ONE SPECIES IN
PARTICULAR THAT'S EVOLVED INTO</i>

00:36:10.401 --> 00:36:13.304 line:0%
<i>SUCH A SKILLED CREATURE,
IT STANDS OUT IN</i>

00:36:13.304 --> 00:36:15.373 line:0%
<i>THE OCTOPUS FAMILY...</i>

00:36:18.075 --> 00:36:20.845 line:0%
<i>THE MIMIC OCTOPUS.</i>

00:36:23.881 --> 00:36:27.852 line:0%
<i>IT CAN IMITATE A POISONOUS
LIONFISH OR LIKE THIS BROWN</i>

00:36:27.852 --> 00:36:31.155 line:0%
<i>MIMIC, BURY ALL BUT TWO OF
ITS ARMS TO LOOK LIKE A HIGHLY</i>

00:36:31.155 --> 00:36:33.391 line:0%
<i>VENOMOUS SEA SNAKE.</i>

00:36:33.391 --> 00:36:36.260 line:0%
<i>HERE, IT MIMICS A FISH
CALLED A BANDED SOLE...</i>

00:36:36.260 --> 00:36:39.230 line:0%
<i>A POISONOUS RELATIVE
OF THE FLOUNDER.</i>

00:36:39.697 --> 00:36:42.934 line:0%
<i>AND IN EACH OF THESE CASES, IT
NOT ONLY COPIES THE APPEARANCE</i>

00:36:42.934 --> 00:36:47.672 line:0%
<i>BUT THE SWIMMING STYLE AND
SPEED OF ITS INSPIRATION.</i>

00:36:49.640 --> 00:36:52.009 line:0%
<i>NO DISCUSSION OF THE OCTOPUS
IS COMPLETE WITHOUT MENTIONING</i>

00:36:52.009 --> 00:36:54.812 line:0%
<i>ITS MOST ICONIC APPENDAGES.</i>

00:36:56.514 --> 00:36:58.849 line:0%
<i>YOU KNOW IT HAS EIGHT
OF THEM BUT DO YOU KNOW</i>

00:36:58.849 --> 00:37:00.685 line:0%
<i>WHAT THEY'RE CALLED?</i>

00:37:01.686 --> 00:37:04.255 line:0%
<i>ARE THEY A, ARMS?</i>

00:37:04.255 --> 00:37:05.790 line:0%
<i>B, LEGS?</i>

00:37:05.790 --> 00:37:08.226 line:0%
<i>OR C, TENTACLES?</i>

00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:11.896 line:0%
<i>PLUS, DOES THIS OCTOPUS
HAVE THE PSYCHIC SKILLS TO</i>

00:37:11.896 --> 00:37:14.298 line:0%
<i>BEAT THE VEGAS ODDS?</i>

00:37:24.342 --> 00:37:26.244 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: THE OCTOPUS...</i>

00:37:26.244 --> 00:37:29.513 line:0%
<i>AN ALIEN WITH EIGHT
FAMOUS APPENDAGES.</i>

00:37:29.513 --> 00:37:32.750 line:0%
<i>BUT ARE THEY ARMS,
LEGS, OR TENTACLES?</i>

00:37:33.651 --> 00:37:36.153 line:0%
<i>THE ANSWER?</i>

00:37:36.354 --> 00:37:39.557 line:0%
<i>AN OCTOPUS'S APPENDAGES
ARE ACTUALLY CALLED "ARMS,"</i>

00:37:39.757 --> 00:37:42.793 line:0%
<i>BECAUSE THEY HAVE SUCKERS
ALL DOWN THEIR LENGTH.</i>

00:37:42.793 --> 00:37:44.762 line:0%
<i>IF THEY WERE TENTACLES,
THEY WOULD ONLY HAVE THEM</i>

00:37:44.762 --> 00:37:46.264 line:0%
<i>ON THEIR TIPS.</i>

00:37:46.264 --> 00:37:49.033 line:0%
<i>JUST ASK ANY SQUID,
WHICH HAVE TENTACLES.</i>

00:37:49.834 --> 00:37:54.038 line:0%
<i>SO OCTOPUSES HAVE EIGHT ARMS
AND ZERO TENTACLES, OR LEGS.</i>

00:37:56.173 --> 00:37:58.609 line:0%
<i>WHICH IS NOT TO SAY THEY
CAN'T USE THOSE ARMS LIKE WE</i>

00:37:58.609 --> 00:38:00.811 line:0%
<i>USE OUR LEGS.</i>

00:38:04.515 --> 00:38:07.518 line:0%
<i>NOW, WE GET BACK TO OUR
BREAKDOWN OF THE OCTOPUS'S</i>

00:38:07.518 --> 00:38:10.154 line:0%
<i>MOST ESSENTIAL
SURVIVAL TOOLS...</i>

00:38:10.554 --> 00:38:13.190 line:0%
<i>AND 8 OF THE MOST
IMPORTANT OF THOSE TOOLS ARE</i>

00:38:13.190 --> 00:38:17.295 line:0%
<i>THOSE ARMS WE WERE
JUST TALKING ABOUT.</i>

00:38:23.334 --> 00:38:25.970 line:0%
<i>THE GIANT PACIFIC OCTOPUS
CAN KEEP A PREDATOR AWAY</i>

00:38:25.970 --> 00:38:29.240 line:0%
<i>WITH AN ARM SPAN
OF UP TO 20 FEET...</i>

00:38:29.740 --> 00:38:32.977 line:0%
<i>THAT'S AS HIGH AS A
TWO STORY BUILDING.</i>

00:38:32.977 --> 00:38:34.845 line:0%
<i>BUT WHAT REALLY ALLOWS
THESE ARMS TO BE SUCH</i>

00:38:34.845 --> 00:38:37.715 line:0%
<i>LIFE SAVING TOOLS?</i>

00:38:38.316 --> 00:38:40.384 line:0%
<i>HUNDREDS OF
INDEPENDENTLY CONTROLLED,</i>

00:38:40.384 --> 00:38:42.486 line:0%
<i>MUSCULAR SUCTION CUPS.</i>

00:38:46.857 --> 00:38:51.028 line:0%
<i>FOR THE GIANT PACIFIC OCTOPUS,
EACH INDIVIDUAL SUCKER CAN</i>

00:38:51.028 --> 00:38:53.564 line:0%
<i>LIFT UP TO 35 POUNDS.</i>

00:38:53.564 --> 00:38:55.700 line:0%
<i>IF YOU ADD IT ALL UP,
THAT'S THEORETICALLY ALMOST</i>

00:38:55.700 --> 00:38:58.469 line:0%
<i>10,000 POUNDS OF
LIFTING-POWER PER ARM...</i>

00:38:59.170 --> 00:39:02.306 line:0%
<i>THE WEIGHT OF A MOVING TRUCK.</i>

00:39:02.506 --> 00:39:05.076 line:0%
<i>BUT THESE SUCTIONS CUPS
AREN'T JUST STRONG...</i>

00:39:05.076 --> 00:39:07.945 line:0%
<i>THEY'RE ALSO "SMART."</i>

00:39:07.945 --> 00:39:10.715 line:0%
ROGER: SO MOST PEOPLE THINK
SUCKERS ARE TO GRAB AND HOLD

00:39:10.715 --> 00:39:12.783 line:0%
THINGS BUT IT'S
MUCH MORE THAN THAT.

00:39:12.783 --> 00:39:15.619 line:0%
SUCKERS ARE A VERY
SOPHISTICATED ORGAN.

00:39:15.619 --> 00:39:17.988 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: LET'S TAKE
A CLOSER LOOK INSIDE THE</i>

00:39:17.988 --> 00:39:20.591 line:0%
<i>SUCTION CUPS OF AN OCTOPUS.</i>

00:39:21.492 --> 00:39:24.462 line:0%
<i>EACH SUCKER IS COVERED IN
SENSITIVE CHEMICAL RECEPTORS</i>

00:39:24.462 --> 00:39:26.831 line:0%
<i>THAT HELP THE OCTOPUS
SENSE THE WORLD AROUND IT,</i>

00:39:27.365 --> 00:39:29.233 line:0%
<i>INCLUDING FOOD.</i>

00:39:29.767 --> 00:39:33.404 line:0%
<i>YES, THE OCTOPUS CAN
TASTE WITH EACH SUCKER.</i>

00:39:34.372 --> 00:39:37.508 line:0%
<i>EACH SUCTION CUP IS LIKE A
TONGUE AND WITH MANY SPECIES</i>

00:39:37.508 --> 00:39:40.378 line:0%
<i>HAVING OVER 200
SUCTION CUPS PER ARM...</i>

00:39:40.378 --> 00:39:45.950 line:0%
<i>THAT'S LIKE EACH OCTOPUS
HAVING OVER 1,600 TONGUES.</i>

00:39:45.950 --> 00:39:49.520 line:0%
<i>SO HOW CAN THE OCTOPUS'S
BRAIN PROCESS THE SIGNALS FROM</i>

00:39:49.520 --> 00:39:53.157 line:0%
<i>1,600 TONGUES, PLUS
EVERYTHING ELSE IT HAS TO DO,</i>

00:39:53.157 --> 00:39:54.792 line:0%
<i>ALL AT ONCE?</i>

00:39:54.792 --> 00:39:56.360 line:0%
<i>THE ANSWER?</i>

00:39:56.360 --> 00:39:58.062 line:0%
<i>IT DOESN'T HAVE TO.</i>

00:39:58.062 --> 00:40:00.898 line:0%
<i>THAT'S BECAUSE THEIR
ARMS DO MUCH OF THE WORK.</i>

00:40:00.898 --> 00:40:03.634 line:0%
<i>EACH OCTOPUS ARM HAS
THREE TIMES AS MANY NEURONS</i>

00:40:03.634 --> 00:40:06.704 line:0%
<i>THAN IN THEIR BRAIN.</i>

00:40:07.471 --> 00:40:09.740 line:0%
<i>IF YOU WERE TO
SEVER THE ARM,</i>

00:40:09.740 --> 00:40:11.642 line:0%
<i>THEN TOUCH A
PIECE OF FOOD TO IT,</i>

00:40:11.642 --> 00:40:13.978 line:0%
<i>THE SEVERED ARM WILL STILL
MOVE THE FOOD TO WHERE THE</i>

00:40:13.978 --> 00:40:17.515 line:0%
<i>MOUTH USED TO BE, EVEN
THOUGH THE HEAD ISN'T THERE...</i>

00:40:17.515 --> 00:40:21.318 line:0%
<i>AND EVEN AN HOUR AFTER
THE ARM'S BEEN SEVERED!</i>

00:40:22.219 --> 00:40:24.789 line:0%
<i>AND THAT'S NOT EVEN CLOSE
TO THE CRAZIEST ONE OF THE</i>

00:40:24.789 --> 00:40:27.324 line:0%
<i>OCTOPUS'S SURVIVAL SKILLS.</i>

00:40:35.232 --> 00:40:38.469 line:0%
<i>EVEN THOUGH THE OCTOPUS CAN
PERFECTLY MATCH THE COLOR OF</i>

00:40:38.469 --> 00:40:42.306 line:0%
<i>THEIR ENVIRONMENT, THEY
CAN'T ACTUALLY SEE COLOR.</i>

00:40:42.306 --> 00:40:44.842 line:0%
<i>THEY'RE COLOR BLIND.</i>

00:40:45.409 --> 00:40:47.645 line:0%
NATALIA: ALL THIS COLOR
CHANGING AND SHAPE SHIFTING

00:40:47.645 --> 00:40:49.413 line:0%
AND THEY'RE COLORBLIND.

00:40:49.413 --> 00:40:51.081 line:0%
IT'S CRAZY...

00:40:51.081 --> 00:40:54.118 line:0%
THESE OCTOPUS, YOU KNOW,
THEY'RE BORN GENIUSES.

00:40:54.385 --> 00:40:57.555 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: SO HOW
DO THEY DO IT?</i>

00:40:58.422 --> 00:41:00.991 line:0%
<i>NEW EVIDENCE SUGGESTS
OCTOPUSES MAY BE DETECTING</i>

00:41:00.991 --> 00:41:04.195 line:0%
<i>COLORS THROUGH THEIR SKIN.</i>

00:41:05.729 --> 00:41:08.599 line:0%
<i>IT'S LIKE THEY'RE SEEING
WITH THEIR ENTIRE BODY.</i>

00:41:09.700 --> 00:41:12.203 line:0%
ROGER: LIGHT DETECTING
MOLECULES IN OTHER ANIMALS

00:41:12.203 --> 00:41:14.905 line:0%
HAVE NEVER BEEN DEMONSTRATED.

00:41:14.905 --> 00:41:17.441 line:0%
IF WE CAN SOMEHOW FIND THAT
THEY HAVE THIS LIGHT SENSING

00:41:17.441 --> 00:41:20.177 line:0%
CAPABILITY TO DO SOMETHING
WITH IT THROUGHOUT THE SKIN,

00:41:20.177 --> 00:41:22.947 line:0%
IT WOULD BE REALLY
NEW TO SCIENCE.

00:41:26.484 --> 00:41:29.119 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: SO THE OCTOPUS
IS STILL TEACHING SCIENCE</i>

00:41:29.119 --> 00:41:31.655 line:0%
<i>SOMETHING NEW EVERY DAY.</i>

00:41:32.256 --> 00:41:35.226 line:0%
<i>BUT ITS MOST WELL KNOWN
SURVIVAL TOOL IS ITS ABILITY</i>

00:41:35.226 --> 00:41:38.095 line:0%
<i>TO DISAPPEAR INTO
A PUFF OF INK.</i>

00:41:47.338 --> 00:41:49.807 line:0%
<i>THERE MAY BE MORE GOING
ON IN THAT CLOUD THAN</i>

00:41:49.807 --> 00:41:52.009 line:0%
<i>ANYONE EVER REALIZED.</i>

00:41:52.009 --> 00:41:53.844 line:0%
ROGER: PEOPLE SEE A
PUFF OF INK AND THEY SAY,

00:41:53.844 --> 00:41:54.979 line:0%
"OH, THAT'S COOL.

00:41:54.979 --> 00:41:56.347 line:0%
THAT'S HOW IT WORKS."

00:41:56.347 --> 00:41:59.750 line:0%
BUT, THERE'S MUCH
MORE TO IT THAN THAT.

00:42:00.718 --> 00:42:03.287 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: SOME OCTOPUS INK
CONTAINS A CHEMICAL CALLED</i>

00:42:03.287 --> 00:42:06.624 line:0%
<i>TYROSINASE WHICH CAN DISRUPTS
AND CONFUSE A PREDATOR'S</i>

00:42:06.624 --> 00:42:10.594 line:0%
<i>SENSES LIKE SMELL AND TASTE.</i>

00:42:10.594 --> 00:42:13.297 line:0%
<i>AT THE SAME TIME, SOME
RESEARCH SHOWS THAT THE INK</i>

00:42:13.297 --> 00:42:16.901 line:0%
<i>MAY ALSO CONTAIN
NEUROTRANSMITTERS WHICH ALERT</i>

00:42:16.901 --> 00:42:20.271 line:0%
<i>OTHER OCTOPUSES THAT THERE'S
A PREDATOR IN THE AREA.</i>

00:42:20.271 --> 00:42:24.742 line:0%
<i>SO ITS NOT JUST SAVING ITSELF
BUT THE SPECIES AS A WHOLE AND</i>

00:42:24.742 --> 00:42:26.777 line:0%
<i>IT GETS MORE AMAZING.</i>

00:42:26.777 --> 00:42:29.480 line:0%
BILL: THEY CAN EXPEL THE
INK IN THE FORM OF SOMETHING

00:42:29.480 --> 00:42:31.715 line:0%
CALLED A "PSEUDO-MORPH."

00:42:31.715 --> 00:42:35.886 line:0%
<i>NARRATOR: HERE'S HOW IT WORKS:
SOMETIMES A FLEEING OCTOPUS</i>

00:42:35.886 --> 00:42:38.856 line:0%
<i>WILL SHOOT OUT A SMALL
BALL OF MUCUS WITH THE INK.</i>

00:42:39.623 --> 00:42:42.159 line:0%
<i>THIS MUCUS SURROUNDS
THE INK FORMING A DARK,</i>

00:42:42.159 --> 00:42:45.195 line:0%
<i>FLOATING SHAPE, OR
"PSEUDO-MORPH" THAT ACTUALLY</i>

00:42:45.195 --> 00:42:48.999 line:0%
<i>RESEMBLES ANOTHER
OCTOPUS THE EFFECT?</i>

00:42:48.999 --> 00:42:51.402 line:0%
<i>A GOOEY GHOST LEFT
HANGING IN THE WATER TO</i>

00:42:51.402 --> 00:42:54.004 line:0%
<i>CONFUSE HUNGRY FISH.</i>

00:42:59.443 --> 00:43:02.179 line:0%
<i>IT TAKES SOME PRETTY SPECIAL
BIOLOGY AND AN EVEN MORE</i>

00:43:02.179 --> 00:43:06.817 line:0%
<i>ADVANCED BRAIN TO PULL OFF
ALL THESE AMAZING ABILITIES.</i>

00:43:08.052 --> 00:43:09.353 line:0%
<i>HOW ADVANCED?</i>

00:43:09.353 --> 00:43:12.089 line:0%
<i>BELIEVE IT OR NOT,
SOME PEOPLE THINK THIS OCEANIC</i>

00:43:12.089 --> 00:43:14.959 line:0%
<i>ALIEN MAY EVEN BE PSYCHIC.</i>

00:43:19.463 --> 00:43:21.465 line:0%
<i>MEET PAUL THE OCTOPUS.</i>

00:43:21.465 --> 00:43:24.568 line:0%
<i>IT SEEMED PAUL HAD A KNACK
